+{"task_id":"task-004","status":"completed","summary":"Implemented checklist-aware core normalization and validation for the Phase 1 container layer, including primitive-shape sanity checks, simulation-bound validation, explicit unsupported-feature errors, normalize-index handling, zero-dimension boundary coercion, and supporting tests/docs.","key_findings":["Added `autofdtd.core.validation` as the shared normalization layer for tagged component payloads, covering name trimming, vector coercion, primitive geometry checks for `Box`/`Sphere`/`Cylinder`, structure-bound checks against the simulation domain, and zero-size-axis boundary coercion to `Periodic`.","`Simulation` now exposes explicit Phase 1 control-policy fields for `normalize_index`, `relax_courant`, `low_freq_smoothing`, and `lumped_elements`, with implemented validation for normalize-index and clear fail-fast errors for deferred or rejected core features.","Unsupported feature handling is now tied directly to the local feature matrix through lookup helpers in `autofdtd.planning`, so deferred and reject-clearly feature tags fail with explicit messages instead of being accepted silently or rejected as unknown extras.","Coverage now includes normalization, primitive shape errors, out-of-domain warnings and errors, zero-dimension absorbing-boundary coercion, normalize-index validation, and planning lookups, with docs and working memory updated to point later tasks at the shared validator path."],"artifacts":[{"path":"src/autofdtd/core/validation.py","description":"Shared Phase 1 validation and normalization helpers for tagged component payloads and simulation-bound checks."},{"path":"src/autofdtd/core/containers.py","description":"Integrated container-level validators for geometry, media, boundaries, normalize-index, and deferred-feature policies."},{"path":"src/autofdtd/planning.py","description":"Added feature lookup helpers and extra tracked Phase 1 feature tags used by validation."},{"path":"tests/test_containers.py","description":"Validation coverage for normalization, shape constraints, unsupported features, domain bounds, and zero-dimension boundary coercion."},{"path":"docs/architecture.md","description":"Architecture notes describing the new shared validation layer and its current responsibilities."},{"path":"phase1/working-memory.md","description":"Distilled task handoff notes for later feature-family tasks to reuse the core validation path."}],"error_summary":"","follow_up_notes":"Verification passed with `ruff check`, `pytest -q`, and `mypy src`. Geometry, material, boundary, source, monitor, and grid tasks should extend `autofdtd.core.validation` rather than duplicating checklist-driven policy checks in each family.","next_action":"none"}
diff --git a/phase1/working-memory.md b/phase1/working-memory.md
index 11bce4700009fdceb6136d6d980ba817f03d69a8..faf6b395466d0eee5ab28850a4b5523bf04b014d
--- a/phase1/working-memory.md
+++ b/phase1/working-memory.md
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
 - `phase1/feature-checklist.md` is now mirrored in code via `src/autofdtd/planning.py` so later tasks can reuse a local feature/status source instead of reparsing markdown.
 - `src/autofdtd/core/containers.py` now holds the first frozen tagged container models for `Structure`, `Scene`, and `Simulation`; `src/autofdtd/api/simulation.py` re-exports them as the public API surface.
 - `src/autofdtd/ir/models.py` now defines the first versioned execution IR, with `ComponentIR`, `StructureIR`, `SceneIR`, `SimulationIR`, and `ExecutionPackageIR` as the transport contract.
+- `src/autofdtd/core/validation.py` now centralizes Phase 1 normalization rules, unsupported-feature checks, primitive geometry sanity checks, simulation-bound checks, and zero-dimension boundary coercion.
 
 ## Decisions
 
@@ -29,9 +30,11 @@
 - Keep the initial container layer serialization-light: `to_payload()`, `to_json_text()`, and `write_json()` are enough for snapshots and handoff, while `task-005` can generalize the shared model base.
 - Use a generic family-tagged component envelope in the IR so Phase 1 can package realistic simulations before every feature family has concrete typed IR classes; later tasks can specialize payloads without changing bundle shape.
 - Bundle packaging is directory-based: `manifest.json` points at a hashed `simulation.json` entrypoint, avoiding self-referential manifest hashing while staying suitable for remote upload or local caching.
+- Core validation is checklist-driven: implemented feature tags pass, deferred or rejected tags fail early with explicit errors, and known primitive geometry payloads validate only when enough fields are present so placeholder tagged dicts can survive until their concrete family tasks land.
 
 ## Task Handoffs
 
 - `task-003` should add versioned IR models under `autofdtd.ir` without coupling them to the public API module layout; it can treat `Simulation.to_payload()` as an interim handoff format, not the final IR contract.
 - Later geometry, material, source, and monitor tasks can plug concrete tagged models into the existing container fields without changing the ordered-container semantics.
 - `task-004` and `task-005` can reuse `ComponentIR.payload` plus the shared IR schema version constants instead of inventing another transport shape.
+- Later geometry, source, monitor, boundary, and grid tasks should route new object models through `autofdtd.core.validation.normalize_component()` or extend its equivalents instead of scattering policy checks across each family.
